# Local secrets must never ride along with a deploy.
#
# The CLI already falls back to .gitignore (which lists .env.local), but this
# is worth stating outright: Next.js loads .env.local in every environment
# except test — production included. So a copy that reached the deployment
# would silently override the Vercel dashboard variables, switching the live
# SMS provider without anyone choosing to. Provider configuration belongs in
# the Vercel environment, not in an uploaded file.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Local dev database — never deploy a copy of it.
customers.db

# Build/test artefacts that Vercel regenerates.
.next
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
